  "etymologyNotes": [
    {
      "s": "makemeahanzi",
      "t": "A tall palace"
    },
    {
      "s": "dong_chinese",
      "t": "Pictograph of a tall building. Similar to 京."
    },
    {
      "s": "shuowen_jiezi",
      "t": "崇也。象臺觀高之形。从冂、口。與倉、舍同意。凡高之屬皆从高。",
      "w": 1
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Pictogram (象形) – a tall building. Compare 京, which however is not a Kangxi radical.\nPossibly from Proto-Sino-Tibetan *m/s-gaw (“head”). Compare with Burmese ခေါင်း (hkaung:, “head”). However, 元 (OC *ŋon, “head”) instead is more likely to be related to this Proto-Sino-Tibetan root given its significant semantic agreement (Schuessler, 2007).\nLikely allofams are 喬 (OC *ɡrew, “tall”), and perhaps 浩 (OC *ɡuːʔ, “vast”) (although the vowels do not agree)."
    }
  ],
  "shuowen": "崇也。象臺觀高之形。从冂、口。與倉、舍同意。凡高之屬皆从高。",
  "shuowenExplanation": "崇. Pictograph depicting the form of 臺觀高. Composed of 冂 and 口. Same concept as 倉、舍. All characters in the 高 category contain 高 as radical.",
